 "notes": "Headline result: red \"This Work\" trace, TOP panel of Fig. 3 (|d_e| vs m_phi), the combined limit from initial + higher-frequency CSO-OCXO and HM-OCXO data via coefficient separation. Extracted from the vector PDF (Limitsproj.pdf) of the arXiv e-print; y-axis calibrated from gridlines (y=28.0px=1e6, 9.5px/decade) and x-axis (x=54.7px=1e-20 eV, 27.55px/decade). Curve downsampled by median in 64 log-mass bins; noisy upward spikes (measurement noise) smoothed. Mass band 4.4e-19 to 6.8e-14 eV matches abstract. The paper is a scalar-DM (dilaton) search; d_e is the fine-structure-constant coupling alpha(phi)=alpha(1+d_e*phi) with dimensionless phi = canonical Damour-Donoghue d_e, so no conversion. rho_DM=0.45 GeV/cm^3 assumed (limit scales as sqrt(rho)). CL=95%. Note: figure minimum |d_e|~1.4 whereas the abstract quotes most-sensitive d_e >= 1.59e-1 (~factor 10 smaller); the digitised compilation curve derives from the figure, so figure values are reported. Paper also bounds |d_me - d_g| (bottom panel), reported here as the secondary combination; d_e is the main ScalarPhoton result.",
